<title>USA: TABLE - Brunswick Corp sells $200 mln notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Brunswick Corp sells $200 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Brunswick Corp was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>Brunswick Corp is a leading maker of pleasure boats, marine engines, also bowling equipment, fishing products and defense products.</p>
<p>BORROWER BRUNSWICK CORP</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.125 PCT  MATURITY 8/1/2027</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.291  FIRST PAY DATE 2/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA1  YIELD 7.183 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-PLUS  SPREAD +83 BPS    MAKE-WHOLE- CALL AT</p>
<p>						  +15 BASIS POINTS OVER</p>
<p>						  THE U.S. TREASURY NOTE</p>
<p>((Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
